U3: 100 = 2x (2x-16 +x). Solve this sum",\(100 = 2x(2x-16+x)\) First simplify inside the brackets: \[ 2x-16+x = 3x-16 \] So \[ 100 = 2x(3x-16) \] Multiply out: \[ 100 = 6x^2 - 32x \] Bring all terms to one side: \[ 6x^2 - 32x - 100 = 0 \] Divide by 2 to make it simpler: \[ 3x^2 - 16x - 50 = 0 \] Factor: \[ 3x^2 - 16x - 50 = (3x-25)(x+2) \],NA,,,,,Academic,,,,1824,64,0.000832,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
