58b5fd11-c574-4bad-b7dc-0eb2b8a90e64,2026-08-15T13:46:57.102Z,1,3,"U1: Explain this question The image asks why a tennis ball is easier to stop than a cricket ball when both are moving at the same velocity. Since momentum equals mass times velocity, the heavier cricket ball has greater momentum and therefore requires more force to stop.
