10c8712a-5762-4a1a-a2c1-1cb9154cf0fd,2026-08-15T13:30:37.104Z,1,6,"U1: A train travels at a speed is 25m/s and covers a distance of 360km. How much time does it take
U2: A train travels 180 km in 3 h. Find itz speed in : (i) km/h (ii) m/s (iii) What distance will it travels in 4h of it maintains the same speed throughout the journey
U3: Step by step
U4: The fastest galloping horse can reach the speed of appro
U5: The fastest galloping horse can reach the speed of approximately 18m/s. How does this compare to the speed of a train moving at 72km/h
U6: Solve it The image shows a table of time and distance values for an object. The task is to determine whether its speed is uniform or non-uniform and calculate its average speed. The distance changes by unequal amounts over equal time intervals, so the motion is non-uniform; the average speed is 60 m","From the table: - Initial time \(=0\ \text{s}\) - Final time \(=100\ \text{s}\) - Total distance \(=60\ \text{m}\) Average speed is: \[ \text{Average speed}=\frac{\text{total distance}}{\text{total time}} =\frac{60}{100} =0.6\ \text{m/s} \] For uniform speed, the object should cover equal distances ",Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,1930,64,0.000874,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
