U11: A matrix which is not symmetric is skew symmetric. Is it right","**No, that’s not right.** For a square matrix \(A\): - **Symmetric** means \(A^T = A\). - **Skew-symmetric** means \(A^T = -A\). If a matrix is **not symmetric** (so \(A^T \ne A\)), it does **not** automatically mean it is skew-symmetric. Many matrices are **neither** symmetric nor skew-symmetric. E",Conceptual,,,,,Academic,,,,1968,62,0.000886,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Concept Explanation,gate_llm,gate_llm
