c7188665-6380-47d8-860e-a0d3d085c70e,2026-08-15T11:20:51.961Z,1,3,"U1: how to solve this question
U2: Q2. Add (a) \( p+p+p+p, p+p+p+k q, p+q+p-q \), \[ \begin{array}{l} =p+p+p+p, p+p+p+p, p+q+p-\alpha \\ =9 p+q \end{array} \] (b) \( p-q+p-q, p+q x \bar{p}+q \) \[ \begin{array}{l} =2 p-3 q+2 q \\ =2 q \end{array} \] (c) \( p+q-(p+q), p-q-p-q \) \[ \begin{array}{l} p+q-p-q+p-q+p-q \\ =-2 q \end{array}
U3: Okay solve first one","**(a) Add:** \(p+p+p+p,\; p+p+p+q,\; p+q+p-q\) I’ll keep it super clear by simplifying each expression first: - \(p+p+p+p = 4p\) - \(p+p+p+q = 3p+q\) - \(p+q+p-q = (p+p) + (q-q) = 2p\) Now add them: \[ 4p + (3p+q) + 2p = (4p+3p+2p) + q = 9p + q \] **Final answer: \(\mathbf{9p+q}\).**",NA,,,,,Academic,,,,1951,64,0.000883,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
