U17: Answer A biology multiple-choice question with a graph of the hemoglobin–oxygen dissociation curve (percentage saturation vs partial pressure of oxygen). The question asks under which condition the curve shifts to the right, with options: rise in pCO2, fall in pH, raise in temperature, or all of the
U18: Answer Multiple-choice biology question asking which statement about carbon dioxide transport, hemoglobin, and blood chemistry is correct.
U19: Answer Multiple-choice biology question asking what a reduction in blood pH will cause, with four physiological options related to blood supply to brain, hemoglobin affinity for oxygen, bicarbonate ion release, and heart rate.","**Answer: (B) decrease the affinity of haemoglobin for oxygen.** When the pH of blood decreases, it becomes more acidic. Hydrogen ions affect haemoglobin so that it holds oxygen less tightly. This helps haemoglobin **release more oxygen to body tissues**. This is called the **Bohr effect**.",Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,2445,64,0.001080,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
