and
\[
a+b+c=2+3+5=10.
\]

So
\[
10+2\sqrt6+2\sqrt{15}+2\sqrt{10}=(\sqrt2+\sqrt3+\sqrt5)^2.
\]

### 4) Take the square root
\[
\sqrt{(\sqrt2+\sqrt3+\sqrt5)^2}=\sqrt2+\sqrt3+\sqrt5
\]
(we take the positive root because \(\sqrt2,\sqrt3,\sqrt5\) are all positive).

