U7: Bookme jesa hai wase hyy sam ja oo mere tbeyet thek nhi thi isliye me school ko nhi ge or sir ne ye wala q samja ya tum mere ko is me ju step by step hai us hy ke trha samjao","## ठीक है—मैं **बुक जैसा step‑by‑step** समझा रहा/रही हूँ (Hindi में)

### दिया है:
\[
\frac{2}{x}-\frac{3}{y}=15 \quad ; \quad \frac{8}{x}+\frac{5}{y}=77
\]

---

## Step 1: मान लो (बुक वाली trick)
\[
m=\frac{1}{x}, \quad n=\frac{1}{y}
\]

अब fractions हट गए, क्योंकि \(\frac{2}{x}=2\cdot\frac{1}{x}=2m\) और \(\frac{3}{y}=3n\)

---

## Step 2: equations को \(m,n\) में लिखो
\[
2m-3n=15 \quad ...(1)
\]
\[
8m+5n=77 \quad ...(2)
\]

---

## Step 3: \(m\) हटाने के लिए (1) को 4 से multiply करो
(क्योंकि (2) में \(8m\) है)

\[
(1)\times 4:\quad 8m-12n=60 \quad ...(3)
\]

---

## Step 4: (2) और (3) को घटाओ
\[
(2)-(3):\quad (8m+5n)-(8m-12n)=77-60
\]
\[
8m+5n-8m+12n=17
\]
\[
17n=17 \Rightarrow n=1
\]

---

## Step 5: \(n=1\) को (1) में रखो
\[
2m-3(1)=15
\]
\[
2m-3=15
\]
\[
2m=18 \Rightarrow m=9
\]

---

## Step 6: अब वापस \(x,y\) निकालो
क्योंकि
\[
m=\frac{1}{x}=9 \Rightarrow x=\frac{1}{9}
\]
और
\[
n=\frac{1}{y}=1 \Rightarrow y=1
\]

---

## Final Answer
\[
\boxed{x=\frac{1}{9},\quad y=1}
\]

यही “बुक वाला” तरीका है: **पहले \(\frac{1}{x},\frac{1}{y}\) को \(m,n\) मानो, फिर linear equations solve करके वापस \(x,y\) निकालो।**",Small Talk,4,4,3,7.333333333333333,Academic | Specific Named Resource | Direct Response | Image Upload | Speech to Text | Blurry / Unclear Image,,,0.9500,16674,349,0.004152,"The bot correctly identified the academic nature and provided detailed step-by-step explanations as requested, despite initial image quality issues. No critical or moderate failures were found; the bot did not push unwanted templates or ignore user corrections. Overall, the session effectively addressed the user's learning intent with minor initial image clarity challenges.",0,full_rate,Academic,Concept Explanation,explicit_frustration | gate_llm,gate_llm
