4.3 Solution of a Quadratic Equation by Factorisation

Consider the quadratic equation \( 2 x^{2}-3 x+1=0 \). If we replace \( x \) by 1 on the HS of this equation, we get \( \left(2 \times 1^{2}\right)-(3 \times 1)+1=0= \) RHS of the equation.
