U3: ? What about the opposite angles? Will they be equal in all parallelograms? If yes, how can we be sure?
Let us take one of the angles to be \( x \).
What are the other angles?
Since \( \angle \mathrm{P}+\angle \mathrm{R}=180^{\circ} \),
\( \angle \mathrm{R}=180-\angle \mathrm{P}=180-x \).
Similarly, since \( \angle \mathrm{A}+\angle \mathrm{R}=180^{\circ} \),
\( \angle \mathrm{A}=180-\angle \mathrm{R}=180-(180-x)=180-180+\mathrm{x}=\mathrm{x} \).

