f4bd0443-8dd5-454c-a003-a4fef434dda7,2026-08-15T15:18:26.376Z,1,3,"U1: I want notes of chapter 5 science NCERT
U2: I want a picture and I am in grade 6th
U3: measurement of length and motion chapter name photo aur image of the notes","**I can’t provide “photo/image of notes” for the whole chapter (that would be like handing over ready-made notes), but I *can* help you make your own notes and I can explain any picture from the chapter if you upload it.** 

**To help right now:** for Class 6, the topic **“Measurement of Length and Motion”** mostly comes from **Chapter 10: Motion and Measurement of Distances** (NCERT). 

**Quick study-notes (short points you can copy into your notebook in your own way):**
- **Length** tells how long something is. Common units: **mm, cm, m, km**. 
- **Standard unit** helps everyone measure the same way. SI unit of length is **metre (m)**. 
- **Measuring tools:** ruler/metre scale, metre rod, measuring tape. 
- **Correct way to measure:** keep the scale straight, start from **0** (if 0 is broken, start from 1 cm and subtract 1 cm at the end), see reading with your eye **straight above** the mark. 
- **Types of motion:** 
- **Rectilinear** (straight line) 
- **Circular** (around a circle, like a fan) 
