U7: - Rutherford's model of an atom (Discovery of nucleus) → Planciery
In 1911, Geiger and Marsden, working under Ernest Rutherford,
tested Thomson's model of the atom through what became famous as
the gold foil experiment. They aimed a narrow beam of alpha
particles at an extremely thin sheet of gold foil. Alpha (symbol \( \alpha \) )
particles are tiny, positively charged particles emitted from certain
radioactive elements.

Rutherford performed the famous \( \alpha \)-particle scattering experiment in order to know the relative positions of electrons and protons in an atom.

Fig. 11 Rutherford's experiment.

Rutherford Experiment (The gold foil experiment) \( \alpha \) particle are charged particles having 2 units of positive charge and 4 units of mass, that is \( \alpha \)-particles \( \left({ }_{2} \mathrm{He}^{4}\right) \) are doubly charged helium atoms ( \( \mathrm{He}^{+2} \) ). He selected a thin foil of a heavy gold metal because it was only 1000 atoms thick. He bombarded the same with high speed alpha ( \( \alpha \) ) particles. Observation from experiment
When fast moving alpha particles strike very thin gold foil in vacuum, it is found that:
- Most of the fast moving \( \alpha \)-particles passed straight through the gold foil, without any deflection from their original path.
- Some of the \( \alpha \)-particles were deflected by the foil by small angles. This deflection from the straight path is called scattering.
- A very few alpha particles got completely rebound on hitting the gold foil and turned back on their path.

Fig. 10 Ernest Rutherford

Яерһа \( \rightarrow \) a \( a \)
THE SPOTLIGHT
Rutherford model is also called as planetary model of atom because it is similar to that of the solar system. As in solar system, different planets are revolving around the sun, similarly, in an atom the electrons are revolving around the nucleus. Thus, electrons were called planatary electrons.

Fig. 12 Planetary model of atom

THE SPOTLIGHT
Rutherford selected a gold foil because he wanted as thin a layer as possible.
\( L \) and gold is the most meablle metal.

