A **Celsius indicator** usually means a **thermometer** or temperature display that shows temperature in **degrees Celsius (°C)**.

- **0°C** = water freezes 
- **100°C** = water boils (at normal air pressure) 
- Common uses: **weather**, **fever temperature**, **cooking**

## General of Alexander
Alexander the Great had **many generals**, not just one. Some of the most famous were:

- **Parmenion** (important senior general early on) 
- **Hephaestion** (close friend and top commander) 
- **Seleucus** and **Ptolemy** (later became rulers of their own kingdoms)

