U3: write the prime numbers of the whole number using the factor tree method by 315 write the prime factor of the following number using the factor three method by using 250 300","**Prime factorization using a factor tree**

For \(250\):
\[
250 = 25 \times 10
\]
\[
25 = 5 \times 5,\quad 10 = 2 \times 5
\]
So,
\[
\mathbf{250 = 2 \times 5 \times 5 \times 5 = 2 \times 5^3}
\]

For \(300\):
\[
300 = 3 \times 100
\]
\[
100 = 10 \times 10,\quad 10 = 2 \times 5
\]
So,
\[
100 = 2 \times 5 \times 2 \times 5 = 2^2 \times 5^2
\]
and
\[
\mathbf{300 = 3 \times 2^2 \times 5^2 = 2^2 \times 3 \times 5^2}
\]",Procedural,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Speech to Text,,,0.9500,12701,269,0.003199,"The bot correctly answered the user's math questions about prime factorization using the factor tree method without any errors or failures. The session is academic with speech-to-text input, and the user did not express dissatisfaction or re-ask due to failure.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,same_intent_reask | paraphrase_reask | near_duplicate_reask | gate_llm,gate_llm
