U7: If 3rd & 8th terms of an arithmetic sequence are 8 and 22 respectively then find a) sum of the first and 10th term. b)sum of 2nd and 9th term. C) sum of first 10 terms","Let the first term be \(a\) and common difference be \(d\). 
Arithmetic sequence: \(a_n = a + (n-1)d\).

Given:
\[
a_3 = a+2d = 8
\]
\[
a_8 = a+7d = 22
\]
Subtract:
\[
(a+7d)-(a+2d)=22-8
\]
\[
5d=14 \Rightarrow d=\frac{14}{5}
\]
Now
\[
a+2\left(\frac{14}{5}\right)=8 \Rightarrow a+\frac{28}{5}=\frac{40}{5}
\]
\[
a=\frac{12}{5}
\]

**(a) Sum of the 1st and 10th terms** 
\[
a_1=a=\frac{12}{5}
\]
\[
a_{10}=a+9d=\frac{12}{5}+9\cdot\frac{14}{5}=\frac{12+126}{5}=\frac{138}{5}
\]
\[
a_1+a_{10}=\frac{12}{5}+\frac{138}{5}=\frac{150}{5}= \mathbf{30}
\]

**(b) Sum of the 2nd and 9th terms** 
\[
a_2=a+d=\frac{12}{5}+\frac{14}{5}=\frac{26}{5}
\]
\[
a_9=a+8d=\frac{12}{5}+8\cdot\frac{14}{5}=\frac{12+112}{5}=\frac{124}{5}
\]
\[
a_2+a_9=\frac{26}{5}+\frac{124}{5}=\frac{150}{5}= \mathbf{30}
\]

**(c) Sum of the first 10 terms** 
\[
S_{10}=\frac{10}{2}\left(2a+(10-1)d\right)
=5\left(2\cdot\frac{12}{5}+9\cdot\frac{14}{5}\right)
\]
\[
=5\left(\frac{24}{5}+\frac{126}{5}\right)
=5\left(\frac{150}{5}\right)= \mathbf{150}
\]

**Answers:** 
\[
\boxed{\text{(a) } 30,\quad \text{(b) } 30,\quad \text{(c) } 150}
\]",Procedural,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Image Upload | Speech to Text,,,0.9800,14700,281,0.003659,"The bot correctly understood and answered the user's arithmetic progression problem with accurate and complete solutions. The conversation included image uploads and speech-to-text inputs, but the bot handled them well without failures. The user re-asked for formatting help but did not express dissatisfaction or rejection of the answers.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,same_intent_reask | paraphrase_reask | multiple_similar_requests | gate_llm,gate_llm
