For the older children’s slide: height \(=3\text{ m}\), angle with ground \(=60^\circ\). 
Let the length of the slide be \(L\).

\[
\sin 60^\circ=\frac{\text{height}}{\text{slide length}}=\frac{3}{L}
\]

\[
\frac{\sqrt3}{2}=\frac{3}{L}
\]

Now cross-multiply:

\[
L=\frac{3}{\sqrt3/2}=3\cdot\frac{2}{\sqrt3}=\frac{6}{\sqrt3}
\]

Rationalize:

\[
L=\frac{6}{\sqrt3}\cdot\frac{\sqrt3}{\sqrt3}=\frac{6\sqrt3}{3}=2\sqrt3\text{ m}
\]

Decimal value:

\[
L=2\sqrt3 \approx 2(1.732)=3.464 \approx \mathbf{3.46\text{ m}}
\]

So the 2nd case length is **\(\mathbf{2\sqrt3\text{ m} \approx 3.46\text{ m}}\)**.",Procedural,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Image Upload,,,0.9500,13647,248,0.003360,"The bot correctly answered the user's academic questions with accurate, step-by-step solutions and addressed the user's clarifications without any failures. There are no detected issues or failures in the conversation, and the user sentiment is neutral without explicit positive or negative feedback.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,explicit_frustration | gate_llm,gate_llm
