### Q1) Convert \(3.75\) into a fraction in simplest form
Write \(3.75\) as \(\frac{375}{100}\) (move the decimal 2 places).
\[
3.75=\frac{375}{100}
\]
Now simplify by dividing top and bottom by \(25\):
\[
\frac{375}{100}=\frac{375\div 25}{100\div 25}=\frac{15}{4}
\]
So the simplest fraction is **\(\mathbf{\frac{15}{4}}\)** (which is also \(3\frac{3}{4}\)).

