**Please type these exact items (just the numbers), and I’ll produce the full journal with calculations + the revised Balance Sheet:**

1) Share capital details 
- Authorised: ₹ ___ (___ shares of ₹ ___ each) 
- Issued/subscribed/called-up: ___ shares of ₹ ___ each, called up ₹ ___ per share 
- Calls in arrears: ₹ ___ (or: ___ shares × ₹ ___)

2) Reserves & liabilities 
- Sundry creditors ₹ ___ 
- Provision for taxation ₹ ___ 
- Any other liabilities (debentures/loans, etc.) ₹ ___

3) Assets (book values) 
- Goodwill ₹ ___ 
- Land & building ₹ ___ 
- Machinery ₹ ___ 
- Stock ₹ ___ 
- Book debts ₹ ___ 
- Preliminary expenses ₹ ___ 
- Cash at bank ₹ ___ 
- P&L balance (debit/credit) ₹ ___ 
- Profit for the year (if shown separately) ₹ ___

4) Scheme details (confirm) 
- Machinery is **overvalued by ₹10,000** (so reduce machinery by ₹10,000), yes/no 
- Forfeit shares with call outstanding (calls in arrears), yes 
- Reduce paid-up capital by **₹3 per share** (face value same), yes 
- Reissue forfeited shares at **₹5 per share** (confirm number of shares reissued = all forfeited?), yes 
- Utilize provision for taxation if necessary, yes

If you prefer not to type, upload a clearer photo: take it straight from above, crop to the Balance Sheet, and make sure the amounts column is sharp.

Once I have those figures, I’ll write the journal like this (with your numbers filled in):

- **(1) Forfeiture**: Share Capital Dr; To Calls in Arrears; To Forfeited Shares 
- **(2) Reduction of paid-up capital by ₹3/share**: Share Capital Dr; To Capital Reduction 
- **(3) Revaluation / write-down machinery**: Capital Reduction Dr; To Machinery 
- **(4) Write off goodwill/prelim/P&L (debit)**: Capital Reduction Dr; To Goodwill/Prelim/P&L 
- **(5) Reissue**: Bank Dr; Forfeited Shares Dr (discount); To Share Capital 
- **(6) Transfer surplus on forfeiture**: Forfeited Shares Dr; To Capital Reserve 
- **(7) Use provision for tax if needed**: Provision for Tax Dr; To Capital Reduction (only if scheme uses it)

