U9: Marie Curie profile","## Marie Curie — Profile

- **Full name:** Marie Skłodowska Curie 
- **Born:** 7 November 1867, Warsaw (then part of the Russian Empire; now Poland) 
- **Died:** 4 July 1934, Passy, France 
- **Field:** Physics and Chemistry 
- **Known for:** Pioneering work on **radioactivity** 
- **Major discoveries:** **Polonium** (named after Poland) and **radium** (1898) 
- **Key achievements:**
- First woman to win a **Nobel Prize**
- Only person to win **Nobel Prizes in two different sciences** (Physics and Chemistry)
- **Nobel Prizes:**
- **Physics (1903):** Work on radiation (shared with Pierre Curie and Henri Becquerel)
- **Chemistry (1911):** Discovery and isolation of radium and polonium 
