**A sharp knife has a very small edge area. For the same applied force, pressure increases when area decreases:**

\[
\text{Pressure}=\frac{\text{Force}}{\text{Area}}
\]

**Therefore, the sharp edge produces greater pressure and cuts the material more easily.**

