Two common possibilities—tell me which one your question is:

1) **There are \(7\) observations** (so “base” means total count \(n=7\)). 
Then the **sum of all observations** is 
\[
\text{sum} = \text{mean}\times n = 38\times 7 = \mathbf{266}.
\]
(If one value is missing, we can find it from this sum.)

2) **“Base 7” means base-7 number system** (less likely for this chapter). 

