**Question 4:** The angles \(4x+40^\circ\) and \(6x-40^\circ\) are complementary.

Complementary angles add to \(90^\circ\):

\[
(4x+40)+(6x-40)=90
\]

Combine like terms:

\[
10x=90
\]

Divide by \(10\):

\[
\boxed{x=9}
\]

Check the angles:

\[
4(9)+40=76^\circ
\]

\[
6(9)-40=14^\circ
\]

\[
76^\circ+14^\circ=90^\circ
\]

So, **\(x=9\)**, and the two angles are **\(76^\circ\) and \(14^\circ\)**.

