a] ARRANGEMENT OF ELECTRONS
Electrons are present - outside the nucleus \& revolve around it. Shells or Energy levels
- Electrons revolve around the nucleus in definite orbits called - 'shells' [the centrifugal force prevents them from falling into the nucleus].
- The shells are also called 'energy levels' since while revolving in a shell an electron possesses - a certain amount of energy.
- The shell closest to the nucleus is called the - K shell [first shell, or number one shell]. The next or second shell is called the - Lshell[secondshellornumbertwoshell]. Following shells or energy levels are
- An electron has - minimum energy in the - K shell or first shell and the energy increases in the order
- K, L, M, N....

