## Factors to keep in mind while selecting a **Sweta / suitable** Maths textbook (high school)
- **Syllabus match:** Fits your board/class (CBSE/ICSE/State) and the latest curriculum.
- **Concept clarity:** Clear explanations, definitions, and step-by-step methods.
- **Good examples:** Enough solved examples before each exercise.
- **Practice variety:** Mixed questions—basic, application, HOTS/challenging, word problems.
- **Accuracy:** Few errors; correct answer key and (ideally) solutions for tough questions.
- **Chapter sequence:** Topics arranged in a logical order; easy to follow for teaching/learning.
- **Language & layout:** Simple language, clear printing, good diagrams/graphs.
- **Real-life links:** Problems connected to daily life (money, measurement, data, etc.).
- **Exam usefulness:** Includes revision exercises, model papers, and board-style questions.
- **Support for teachers/students:** Summary points, formulas list, tips, and common mistakes.

## Importance of Maths in the school curriculum
- **Builds logical thinking:** Helps students reason and make decisions.
- **Improves problem-solving:** Teaches how to break a problem into steps.
- **Useful in daily life:** Time, money, shopping, measurement, planning.
- **Foundation for many subjects:** Needed for science, computers, economics, and more.
- **Develops accuracy and discipline:** Encourages careful work and checking.
- **Supports future careers:** Important for engineering, technology, finance, research, and many jobs.

