## 1. Decide your priority

For Class 11 in India, usually:

- **High priority:** Physics, Chemistry, Maths / Bio, Computer 
- **Medium:** English 
- **Other subjects:** according to your stream

---

## 2. Sample Daily Timetable (Outside School)

### Before School (30–45 min)
- **Revision only** 
- 15–20 min: Revise formulas (Maths/Physics) 
- 15–20 min: Revise definitions (Chem/Computer)

---

### After School

#### Slot 1 – Subject 1 (1–1.5 hrs)
- Mon/Wed/Fri: **Physics** 
- Tue/Thu/Sat: **Maths** or **Biology**

#### Short Break – 10 min

#### Slot 2 – Subject 2 (1–1.5 hrs)
- Mon/Wed/Fri: **Chemistry** 
- Tue/Thu/Sat: **Computer Science**

#### Short Break – 10 min

#### Slot 3 – Light Subject (45–60 min)
- **English / other subject** (reading + 1 writing task or Q/A)

#### Slot 4 – Mixed Revision (30–45 min)
- 10–15 min: Revise what you studied that day 
- 10–15 min: 4–5 MCQs from old topics 
- 10–15 min: Look at 1–2 weak areas

---

## 3. Weekly Plan

- **Sunday:**
- 1–2 hrs: Full revision of the week 
- 1 hr: Practice test (any one subject) 
- Rest of the day: Relax / hobbies

---

