## Section A: Permutation & Combination (Q1–Q10)

1) Number of ways to arrange the letters of **“ASSASSIN”** is: 
A) 420 B) 630 C) 840 D) 1260

2) Number of 5-digit numbers (no repetition) formed from digits 1–9 that are divisible by 5 is: 
A) 0 B) 1680 C) 3024 D) 1344

3) A committee of 4 is formed from 6 boys and 5 girls, with at least 2 girls. Number of ways: 
A) 120 B) 150 C) 165 D) 180

4) Number of solutions in non-negative integers of \(x+y+z=10\): 
A) 55 B) 66 C) 44 D) 121

5) From 10 people, number of ways to choose a captain and vice-captain: 
A) 45 B) 90 C) 100 D) 10

6) Number of diagonals in a 12-sided polygon: 
A) 54 B) 60 C) 66 D) 72

7) Number of ways to arrange 5 boys and 5 girls in a line so that girls are together: 
A) \(5!\cdot 6!\) B) \(5!\cdot 5!\cdot 2\) C) \(6!\cdot 5!\) D) \(10!/5!\)

8) Number of ways to distribute 8 identical chocolates among 4 children (each can get 0 or more): 
A) 35 B) 56 C) 45 D) 84

9) If \(^{n}C_{r}=^{n}C_{r+1}\), then \(n\) equals: 
A) \(2r\) B) \(2r+1\) C) \(r+1\) D) \(r\)

10) Number of 3-letter words (meaningless allowed) from A–Z without repetition that start with a vowel: 
A) 5×25×24 B) 21×25×24 C) 5×26×25 D) 5×25×25

---

