U6: Sahi se btao","**सबसे छोटी संख्या \(N\) ऐसी चाहिए कि 16, 36 और 40 से भाग देने पर हर बार शेष \(5\) बचे।**

इसका मतलब है कि \(N-5\) इन तीनों से **पूरा-पूरा विभाज्य** होगा:
\[
N-5 \text{ 16, 36, 40 का गुणज होगा}
\]
इसलिए
\[
N-5=\text{LCM}(16,36,40)
\]

अब LCM निकालते हैं:

\[
16=2^4,\quad 36=2^2\times 3^2,\quad 40=2^3\times 5
\]

LCM में हर prime का **सबसे बड़ा घात** लेते हैं:
\[
\text{LCM}=2^4\times 3^2\times 5=16\times 9\times 5=720
\]

अब
\[
N = 720 + 5 = 725
\]

जांच: 
\(725\div 16\) में शेष \(5\) (क्योंकि \(16\times 45=720\)) 
\(725\div 36\) में शेष \(5\) (क्योंकि \(36\times 20=720\)) 
\(725\div 40\) में शेष \(5\) (क्योंकि \(40\times 18=720\))

**इसलिए सबसे छोटी संख्या \(\mathbf{725}\) है।**",Conceptual,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Image Upload,,,0.9500,13425,250,0.003318,"The bot correctly understood and answered the user's math questions, including the one from the uploaded image, without any factual or procedural errors. There were no failures in context handling or inappropriate template use. The user rephrased a question once but did not indicate frustration or rejection, so user sentiment is neutral.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,explicit_frustration | gate_llm,gate_llm
