EXAMPLE 13. Suppose \( l, m \) and \( n \) are three lines in the same plane such that 1 of Frefact line I intersects \( m \), then prove that \( l \) intersect \( n \) also.

Solution. Here, the lines \( l, m \) and \( n \) lie in the same plane such that \( l \) intersects \( m \) and \( n \| m \).

We have to prove that line \( l \) intersects \( n \) also.
If possible, let \( l \) does not intersects the line \( n \).
Then, \( l \| n \).

But \( m \| n \) (Given)
Hence, \( l \| m \). [ ∵ Lines which are parallel to the same line are parallel to each other]
But it is given that \( l \) intersects \( m \), which is a contradiction.
Thus, our assumption that \( l \) does not intersect \( n \) is wrong.
Hence, \( l \) intersects \( n \) also.
