## Public Deposit (Meaning)
A **public deposit** is money that a company **accepts (borrows)** from the **general public** for a **fixed period** and **pays interest** on it. It is a way for a company to raise **short/medium-term finance**.

## Key points
- Taken as **fixed deposits** from people (not from banks)
- **Interest** is paid to depositors
- Used to meet **working capital** and other business needs
- Considered **short-term or medium-term**, depending on the time period

