## Expansion of the idea: **“A bad workman blames his tools.”**
The proverb “A bad workman blames his tools” means that a person who lacks skill or does not work carefully often gives excuses for failure. Instead of accepting mistakes, such a person says the tools were of poor quality or the conditions were not right. But in truth, tools are only helpers; the most important thing is the worker’s training, attention, and practice. A good workman learns to use even ordinary tools properly and finds ways to improve the result. For example, a student who has not studied well may blame a pen, bad handwriting, or a difficult paper, but the real problem is poor preparation. Blaming tools may save a person from embarrassment for a moment, yet it prevents real improvement. This proverb teaches us to be responsible, learn from our faults, and focus on developing our skills instead of making excuses.",Conceptual,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Not Math/Science | Specific Named Resource,,,0.9500,12896,291,0.003217,"The bot consistently provides relevant and accurate expansions of the idea as requested by the user, addressing the academic intent without any failures. There are no indications of bot failures or user dissatisfaction, though the user rephrased the request multiple times without explicit complaint. Overall, the session is successful and reliable.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,drop_off | gate_llm,gate_llm
