U10: it doesnt show anything so u teach me","Text file handling in Python is basically **open → read/write → close** (and `with open(...)` closes automatically). The main things you need are file **modes** (`'r'`, `'w'`, `'a'`) and the common methods **`read()`**, **`readline()`**, **`readlines()`**, **`write()`**.

### Open (best way)
```python
with open(""file.txt"", ""r"") as f:
data = f.read()
```

### Read
```python
f.read() # whole file as one string
f.readline() # one line
f.readlines() # list of all lines
```

### Write / Append
```python
with open(""file.txt"", ""w"") as f:
f.write(""Hello\n"") # overwrite file

with open(""file.txt"", ""a"") as f:
f.write(""More\n"") # add at end
```

If “it doesn’t show anything” usually means one of these:
- you used `'w'` mode (it clears the file)
- you forgot to `print()` what you read
- file path/name is wrong

