U31: explain transaction number 6 and 7 I think it's wrong because the entry will be cash to Srijan because is coming in and region is the given I think the transaction number 6 is wrong","You’re right to question it — the **side** is correct (it’s coming in), but the **wording** matters.

## ✅ Transaction 6: “Received cheque from Srijan ₹6,200”
Since the cheque is **received**, it is an **inflow**.

- If it is **not said** “deposited into bank same day”, it is treated as **cheques in hand** and entered in the **Cash column** (on the **debit/receipts side**).

**Correct cash book entry (Receipts side):** 
**To Srijan A/c — Cash ₹6,200**

So it’s **not “Cash to Srijan”**. In the cash book, we write **“To Srijan”** on the debit side (cash coming in).

## ✅ Transaction 7: “Endorsed Srijan’s cheque in favour of Adit”
Endorsed = you **gave that same cheque** to Adit to settle what you owe him.

So it becomes an **outflow** in the cash book (still using the Cash column if you’re treating it as cheque-in-hand).

**Correct cash book entry (Payments side):** 
**By Adit A/c — Cash ₹6,200**

## Key idea (why this works)
- **T6 adds** ₹6,200 to “cheques in hand” (cash column).
- **T7 removes** the same cheque when you pass it to Adit.
- Net cash effect becomes zero, but both events are recorded.

If your school/book follows the rule **“endorsed cheques are not entered in cash book”**, then **T7 would go to the journal instead**.",Procedural,1,1,1,2,Academic | Image Upload | Speech to Text,,Incorrect Answer | Correction Ignored,0.9500,20763,364,0.005046,"The session is academic with multiple image uploads and speech-to-text inputs. The bot gave several incorrect answers due to misreading or miscalculating data and failed to fully address user corrections, resulting in repeated errors and unresolved confusion. This led to moderate user frustration and lowered scores across all axes.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,explicit_frustration | gate_llm,gate_llm
